  "name": "Sentinel-1 launch",
  "description": "Sentinel-1A and 1C launched from Vandenberg on Falcon 9 a few days before the study's precise orbits start (not the real dates): each lifts off southbound into the plane it will fly, is left at 600 km, and with three burns of its own thrusters (a phasing burn, an aimed transfer and an arrival burn) reaches the place ESA's precise orbit puts it at 00:00:02 UTC on 1 July 2025, from where the study begins. From then on each keeps within 50 m of its ground tracks with small along-track burns. Watch the PHASING rows settle at 176 deg once both have arrived.",
